<speak>That sounds like a healthy practical distinction for your schedule. We can avoid placing ordinary relationship calls into the time you have set aside for yourself and your family. If you have a preferred general window, we can use it as a starting point when arranging future conversations, without assuming it is always free. A little advance notice is usually more considerate than calling unexpectedly and hoping to catch you. You also do not need to return a routine scheduling message immediately. It is perfectly workable for you to deal with those when you are next reviewing your own calendar.</speak>